 34P  c  1994Fo04: a 167-MeV {+37}Cl beam was produced from the Argonne Tandem  
 34P 2c  Linac Accelerator System (ATLAS). Targets were 1 mg/cm{+2} 98.1%       
 34P 3c  enriched {+160}Gd backed by 15 mg/cm{+2} gold. |g rays were detected   
 34P 4c  using the Argonne-Notre Dame BGO |g-ray facility consisting of 12      
 34P 5c  Compton-suppressed Ge detectors and a 50-element bismuth germanate     
 34P 6c  (BGO) array. Measured E|g, I|g, and |g|g-coin. Deduced levels.         
 34P 7c  |g|g-coin gates were placed on known |g rays in specific A|?160        
 34P 8c  products to select individual reaction channels and identify coincident
 34P 9c  |g rays in light product partners. |g|g-correlation matrices produced  
 34P Ac  with the fold condition 4 |< k |< 9 were found to include most of the  
 34P Bc  events associated with deep inelastic processes.                       
